            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital stay of your 48-year-old female patient, admitted on 17 February 2021 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection presenting as COVID-19 pneumonia. Diagnosis was established by PCR testing and chest imaging demonstrating bilateral infiltrates. The patient required supplemental oxygen therapy throughout her stay. Blood tests, arterial blood gas analyses, and continuous pulse oximetry were performed to monitor her respiratory status. She was treated with dexamethasone and anticoagulation therapy. Physiotherapy was initiated early to support respiratory recovery. Her condition improved steadily, and she was discharged on 01 March 2021 in recovering condition. At discharge, she was haemodynamically stable with improving oxygen saturation on room air. Please ensure follow-up including repeat chest imaging in approximately six weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
